# Variant build manifest: read by the generic build script (docker-build/.github/workflows/projects.yml).
# One variant per line: <tag prefix>|<apt tool list to install for this prefix (space-separated)>|<npm global package list (optional, space-separated)>|<uv install flag (1=install/empty=skip)>
# The build script builds and pushes 4 tags per variant:
#   <image>:<prefix>-<version> / <image>:<prefix>-latest (one pair each on Docker Hub and GHCR)
# Pass --build-arg DEV_TOOLS=<prefix> at build time; the Dockerfile reads from this file by prefix:
#   column 2 -> apt-get install; column 3 -> npm install -g (e.g. pnpm, required by the dsh-market plugin marketplace);
#   column 4 = 1 -> install uv via the official install.sh (Python package manager, needed by MCP's uvx/uv run launch modes)
# To add or remove tools, just edit the lines below; no changes to the build script or Dockerfile are needed.
# Special prefix test: besides installing the tools below, the Dockerfile also installs an extra
# dsh plugin after DSH is installed (dsh plugin --profile web add github:smanx/dsh-conversation-indicator#main).
test|git curl wget nano jq procps ca-certificates unzip vim openssh-client zip htop tmux tree openssl python3 build-essential bash-completion|pnpm|1
admin|git curl wget nano jq procps ca-certificates unzip vim openssh-client zip htop tmux tree openssl python3 build-essential bash-completion|pnpm|1
devtools|git curl wget nano jq procps ca-certificates unzip vim openssh-client zip htop tmux tree openssl python3 build-essential bash-completion|pnpm|1
devtools-min|git curl wget nano jq procps ca-certificates unzip|pnpm|1
# admin variant: preinstalls the latest DSH (@next, packaged with the image, works out of the box) by default; the admin console can still install/switch versions and configure the npm registry.
# python3/build-essential must be kept (the admin console compiles the native module node-pty when installing other DSH versions at runtime);
# this variant's runtime entry is the manager service (entrypoint.sh dispatches based on the /app/.admin-mode marker).
